  "caption": "Quinn's road trip came with a deep ache right under the sitting bone. A hill run poked the same spot, and stretching it harder only made it crankier.\n\nThis kind of pain is often an overloaded high hamstring tendon. It's usually about capacity, not tightness, and deep stretches can compress the tendon further.\n\nWhat can help: a cushion or wedge for sitting for a few weeks, gentle isometric holds to calm it, then progressive strength such as bridges, hamstring curls and Romanian deadlifts. Hills and speed come last, and 3–6 months is a common timeframe.\n\nGet it assessed after a sudden pull while sprinting, or if you notice tingling down the leg.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
